{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing","id":442023,"title":"penalty to socializing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-14T18:01:29-07:00","id":442023,"title":"penalty to socializing?","content":"In 1e there was a penalty to social rolls as your primal urge went up , in 2e i don't see it on the chart, or anywhere else (briefly skimmed chapter 3). Can someone correct me if I'm wrong?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:09:07-07:00","id":442045,"title":"","content":"It is not present. There is no such penalty in Second Edition.<br /> <br /> Fortunately!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T18:17:36-07:00","id":442049,"title":"","content":"I agree, I loved 1e, but i always enjoy playing social characters, which 1e werewolves were...not at all.<br /> <br /> I'm glad they changed that up.Now you can be charismatic to people before ripping them apart <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T09:48:19-07:00","id":442702,"title":"","content":"It just takes some effort tin 1st Edition. Nothing stops a character form doing it other than that character's own limitations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:24:27-07:00","id":442765,"title":"","content":"It was still annoying to have to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T06:50:35-07:00","id":444125,"title":"","content":"We have specifically removed the social penalty from Primal Urge in the second edition, yes. It is entirely by design that it is absent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T15:17:19-07:00","id":444970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=442765#post442765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was still annoying to have to deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>One Person's Annoyance is another Person's Challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T19:47:35-07:00","id":445240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=444970#post444970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One Person's Annoyance is another Person's Challenge. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>When marketing to a huge number of people, annoyances are <u><i><b>dangerous</b></i></u>. =P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T03:50:49-07:00","id":448983,"title":"","content":"It was a crutch to carry, and we houseruled it out of the game in 1E.<br /> In the 2E im happy to see it gone, esecially with the social maneuvering of opening doors.*sigh*<br /> Not a fan of the doors-system, but I guess you cant please everyone? ;-)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:30:36-07:00","id":449248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephraim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=448983#post448983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was a crutch to carry, and we houseruled it out of the game in 1E.<br /> In the 2E im happy to see it gone, esecially with the social maneuvering of opening doors.*sigh*<br /> Not a fan of the doors-system, but I guess you cant please everyone? ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>How often do you use forcing doors? Or using soft leverage to raise the impression level to a point where you can roll at hour or turn intervals? In my experience, most people's big beef with Social Maneuvering in 2e is the long intervals at average to good impression levels. Realistically though, if you go into trying to maneuver someone totally cold, you're not going to get results right away, unless you pressure them (force doors).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:36:57-07:00","id":449254,"title":"","content":"It's realistic. <br /> <br /> <i>Too</i> realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T07:55:49-07:00","id":449270,"title":"","content":"That's understandable. Real life is a very poorly designed game. You could just rule that a failed forcing doors attempt doesn't prevent you from using social maneuvering on that character again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:45:08-07:00","id":449309,"title":"","content":"Do you use the doors system, Charlaquin?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:49:03-07:00","id":449315,"title":"","content":"I do, but I'm pretty generous with allowing the players to raise the impression level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T08:59:06-07:00","id":449325,"title":"","content":"How does it work in regards to RP? I've never used it, it looks complicated, but I've been eyeing it over as a possibility. It's not just rolling for wins and losses, right? You RP out your attempts, and that works towards opening doors? Or has it become more 'I offer a bribe for soft leverage,' followed by a roll of the dice?<br /> <br /> I get that that's going to be a table-by-table thing but so far I don't think I've heard of anyone who uses it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:30:34-07:00","id":449368,"title":"","content":"I use it for my Werewolf game; anyone listening to our podcasts will note that it's been used twice so far, once to try and convince Hector the drug-crazed Wolf-Blooded to let the pack in to talk to him (which worked because the Irraka used Primal Allure) and later on an ongoing basis to try and convince him to move to the pack's property so they can check what actually happens to him under the full moon (rolls happening once per day, only one Door left before he acquiesces).<br /> <br /> They all get roleplayed around in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T09:42:16-07:00","id":449397,"title":"","content":"I'm only on the second one, but I'll keep my ears open. It really just seems like a more thought out version of what we've been doing, RPing the socialization and adding a roll, but the Doors make it not so hit or miss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:07:38-07:00","id":449437,"title":"","content":"I'm really happy to see a more formal long-term socializing system in WoD. Before, it was really sensitive to DM fiat. Now DMs can set some doors and I can decide how much I want to invest into convincing X person of Y thing.<br /> <br /> I'll press for Door usage much more strongly in my upcoming WW game, because I think it's easy to fall into the trap of RPing all the conversations and not fully taking into account how crap that NPC should actually be at manipulation or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5292-flailbot","name":"FlailBot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:38:19-07:00","id":449460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=449325#post449325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does it work in regards to RP? I've never used it, it looks complicated, but I've been eyeing it over as a possibility. It's not just rolling for wins and losses, right? You RP out your attempts, and that works towards opening doors? Or has it become more 'I offer a bribe for soft leverage,' followed by a roll of the dice?<br /> <br /> I get that that's going to be a table-by-table thing but so far I don't think I've heard of anyone who uses it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on the player. For those who enjoy acting out their character, I'll engage them in in-character dialogue for a bit, adjudicate an impression level and an appropriate attribute + skill, and ask for the roll. For my players who are less comfortable with that kind of roleplay, I'll ask them to describe in general terms what their character is doing to try to convince the NPC to do what they want, and determine impression level and attribute + skill based on that. If the group is in a hurry and the impression level is anything less than excellent, they'll usually opt to make it a forcing doors roll. Otherwise, depending on the Impression level and how soon they need what ever they're trying to get from the NPC, they'll either leave it there and come back later, or we might fast forward through the interval if the party has nothing else they want to do during that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T10:46:16-07:00","id":449468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=449437#post449437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll press for Door usage much more strongly in my upcoming WW game, because I think it's easy to fall into the trap of RPing all the conversations and not fully taking into account how crap that NPC should actually be at manipulation or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>As somebody generally unsatisfied with only role-playing conversations out, I endeavor to make use of the Social Maneuvering system whenever appropriate: I'll still stick to a basic &quot;Roll and done&quot; if you're asking for minor favors or for something that the person isn't opposed to in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T11:17:47-07:00","id":449491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FlailBot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=449437#post449437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll press for Door usage much more strongly in my upcoming WW game, because I think it's easy to fall into the trap of RPing all the conversations and not fully taking into account how crap that NPC should actually be at manipulation or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually don't let players &quot;roleplay through&quot; things, unless the task is trivially easy or has no interesting consequences for failure. The roleplay helps me determine what roll to call for.<br /> <br /> My policy for task resolution in any RPG is: the player describes or acts out an action, then the GM determines if the outcome of that action is uncertain, and if a chance of failure makes the scene more dramatically interesting. If (and only if) both of those things are true, the GM decides based on the player's description or roleplay what dice roll is appropriate to determine the success or failure of the action, and the consequences of success or failure on the roll, and relays this information to the player. A failed roll does not have to mean the player fails to achieve their goal, but it should add some sort of setback or complication. The player makes the roll, and the GM narrates the results.<br /> <br /> If the players &quot;roleplay through&quot; a social interaction without making any rolls in my games, it's either because there was no chance of them failing anyway, or because the risk of failure would not have made the story more interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-19-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T21:27:54-07:00","id":458653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=449460#post449460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends on the player. For those who enjoy acting out their character, I'll engage them in in-character dialogue for a bit, adjudicate an impression level and an appropriate attribute + skill, and ask for the roll. For my players who are less comfortable with that kind of roleplay, I'll ask them to describe in general terms what their character is doing to try to convince the NPC to do what they want, and determine impression level and attribute + skill based on that. If the group is in a hurry and the impression level is anything less than excellent, they'll usually opt to make it a forcing doors roll. Otherwise, depending on the Impression level and how soon they need what ever they're trying to get from the NPC, they'll either leave it there and come back later, or we might fast forward through the interval if the party has nothing else they want to do during that time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with you. Sometimes it might even be a case of player ability versus PC ability. <br /> <br /> In a current game, the most &quot;social&quot; PC is played by our least socially adept player. She had a lot of frustration at first because of the difficulty to roleplay her character because social mechanics don't come to her easily. With Social Maneuvering, she now simply states what her goal is, how she presents herself, and what she does to get what she wants. (It also helps to remind her to use Bribes and Vices to get better results) Once that is done, our ST will grossly play out the resulting social interaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4990-de_k47","name":"De_K47","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4990_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T22:45:21-07:00","id":458699,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you have to take player skill, comfort, and interest into play. I'm an actor, so I love getting into character and role playing scenes in detail (both as an ST and on the rare occasion that I get to play in someone else's game). But some people don't enjoy that aspect; they may be into RPGs for other reasons, and I'm totally cool with that. Some others may have the interest but lack the experience or social skills. For those players I usually encourage them to push their own comfort zones, but I don't pressure them to do more than they feel brave enough to try.<br /> <br /> I think Nofather's question was more about how the system works within the flow of gameplay, but I assume I answered that to his satisfaction as he hasn't asked for clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T03:24:50-07:00","id":462060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/442023-penalty-to-socializing?p=449248#post449248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How often do you use forcing doors? Or using soft leverage to raise the impression level to a point where you can roll at hour or turn intervals? In my experience, most people's big beef with Social Maneuvering in 2e is the long intervals at average to good impression levels. Realistically though, if you go into trying to maneuver someone totally cold, you're not going to get results right away, unless you pressure them (force doors).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but it depends a bit.<br /> It is hard to say how many times we use forcing doors per story or session. Maybe on average one or two times per story / session.<br /> <br /> When forcing doors I normally penalize the player with some form of resistance from the NPC (if he/she got any). A tough roll would be -3, it is very player driven. I normally add the penalties and let them get on with the rolls and prepare for the &quot;shit hits the fan&quot; scenarios.<br /> <br /> Yesterday we played a story where main character Wolfblooded got into a tough situation with a drug-runner on another packs turf.<br /> She wanted some money that had been stolen off one of the humans in the extended pack. So she meets this Drug-runner out in a partied out ranch in the middle of nowhere.<br /> Now she has backup, but decides to go straight up and bully the guy.<br /> This one was a bit tough for me, as i knew the NPC could get really pissed and the scenario could lead to a lot of combat, and quite possibly some deaths, mainly on the players side.<br /> I asked if this was what she wanted before rolling the dices.She goes hell yes.<br /> Now her character is quite strong socially, but I penalized her for a couple of things:<br /> 1 they are on another packs turf, bullying their puppet.<br /> 2 this pack hates the player-controlled pack<br /> 3 She is forcing a door with physical threats of violence that (most likely) she cant back up.<br /> <br /> I let her roll and she gets 5 success!<br /> <br /> The drug-runner caves in and gives back the money.<br /> I write in my notes he is &quot;soft-hearted&quot; as a home-made condition. He lets the player go.<br /> It feels like we were playing one of those hail mary scenes from Breaking bad.<br /> Now the Drug-runner is not gonna forget this. He will try to get back on the player for this. She might have gotten a dangerous rival in the long run and she has trashed one of the potential connections the pack use to move dangerous shit in and out of the turf. The Drug-runner goes from being potential ally on enemy turf to a full blown nemesis for player character.<br /> <br /> Beats are dropped.<br /> Player loved it. I must say it was the best use of a forced door we have had up until now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T06:00:05-07:00","id":462145,"title":"","content":"Sometimes bluffing pays up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}